    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-028: CSS Grid Layout (Basic)** — `display: grid` + fixed/fr tracks + `minmax` + named areas + gaps.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~350-400 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## The measurement correction worth naming\n\nMy earlier framing was \"grid is only 1.5% of @media layout properties — the real subsystems are position (52%) and flex (31%).\"\n\n**That framing was wrong**, and the correction matters because it changes the ADR priority entirely.\n\n**The mistake**: I counted layout declarations **inside @media blocks**. But the sidebar / content / footer page layout isn't in @media — it's in a **top-level rule** that always matches at any viewport:\n\n```css\n.mw-page-container-inner {\n    display: grid;\n    column-gap: 24px;\n    grid-template-columns: 12.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);\n    grid-template-areas: 'siteNotice siteNotice'\n                        'columnStart pageContent'\n                        'footer footer';\n}\n```\n\nThat's the entire sidebar mechanism. **Two rules on one container.** They parse today, they win the cascade today, they carry correct property values today. The layout engine just doesn't consume `display: grid` — its `Display` enum is only `Block`/`Inline`/`None`.\n\n**Every sidebar-positioning rule ADR-025 through ADR-027 was building toward has been in the cascade since ADR-025.** The layout engine was the only missing piece. My @media-scoped measurement missed this because it measured the wrong scope.\n\nDocumenting the correction in the ADR Context section is itself a Meta-lesson-v4 candidate: *measuring the right count inside the wrong scope produces the wrong priority.* Same discipline that's caught each previous prediction miss.\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n- **`Display::Grid`** added to the enum.\n- **`grid-template-columns` / `grid-template-rows`**: fixed `rem`/`px`, `Nfr`, `minmax(0 | length, Nfr | length)`.\n- **`grid-template-areas`**: named cell map.\n- **`grid-template` shorthand**: expands to longhand at parse time (matches ADR-012 pattern).\n- **`column-gap` / `row-gap` / `gap`** (already length-resolved by ADR-013).\n- **Per-child `grid-area`**: captured from each child's ComputedStyle.\n- **`layout_grid()`**: track sizing, cell assignment, child layout within cells, row height accumulation + gaps.\n- **`layout_element` dispatch**: `display == Grid` → `layout_grid`.\n\n## The three load-bearing design decisions\n\n### 1. `grid-template-areas` is REQUIRED, not just auto-flow\n\nAuto-flow with Wikipedia's 4 children in a 2×3 grid gives:\n- `siteNotice` → row 1 col 1 (not spanning both columns)\n- `columnStart` → row 1 col 2 (wrong row — sidebar is in the content row)\n- `pageContent` → row 2 col 1 (wrong column — content is in the sidebar column)\n- `footer` → row 2 col 2 (not bottom span)\n\n**Wrong layout.** Named areas are the only correct implementation. This is a **correctness requirement**, not an optimization.\n\n### 2. `fr` rows degrade to auto\n\nCSS spec: `fr` rows fill remaining container height. Our `layout()` is flow-oriented — container height = sum of children heights, no parent-height allocation. There's no \"remaining height\" to fill.\n\nDocumented v1 limitation. Visually identical for vertical flow grids (which is what Wikipedia's is). Fixed-height grid containers are rare in modern web.\n\n### 3. Grid-only, deferring flex and position\n\n`@media`-scoped counts suggested flex (41) > grid (2). But grid produces the **larger single visible delta** — one container, one big structural transformation. Flex produces several small ones (header, TOC, toolbar). Leverage over count.\n\nDeferred:\n- **ADR-029 (flex)** — header bar, TOC, toolbar layout.\n- **ADR-030 (position + float)** — overlays, thumbnails, content-embedded elements.\n\n## Meta-lesson-v3 applied\n\nPer ADR-027's three-path framework:\n\n| Path | Status |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Parse `display: grid`? | ✅ (raw string in ComputedStyle since ADR-025) |\n| 2. Win cascade? | ✅ (`.mw-page-container-inner` is top-level) |\n| 3. Get consumed by layout? | ❌ (layout_element drops it) |\n\n**ADR-028 closes path 3.** Predicted visible delta: **high** — sidebar becomes 12.25rem left column, article content fills remaining width, footer spans bottom. Largest single visual delta since ADR-025.\n\n**Honest caveat**: if grid ships and the sidebar still doesn't shift, one of the earlier paths failed in a way this measurement didn't catch (e.g. per-child `grid-area` not in ComputedStyle, or another rule wins on the container). Commit 2's screenshots reveal it honestly.\n\n## Scope estimate (larger than the last three ADRs)\n\n| ADR | Lines | Shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| 025 (external CSS) | ~250 | Single parser + fetch feature |\n| 026 (var()) | ~250 | Single parser feature |\n| 027 (@media) | ~250 | Single parser feature |\n| **028 (grid)** | **~350-400** | **Whole subsystem** |\n\nGrid is categorically different — it's not a parser feature, it's a **layout-engine subsystem**. The estimate reflects that.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **The measurement correction is accepted** — the earlier \"grid 1.5%\" claim measured the wrong scope (@media-scoped counts missed the top-level `.mw-page-container-inner` rule). Comfortable with the revised priority (grid before flex despite flex's higher @media-scoped count)?\n- [ ] **`grid-template-areas` as correctness requirement** — is this the right call, or should v1 ship auto-flow only and defer named areas?\n- [ ] **`fr` rows degrade to auto** — the flow-layout constraint documented. Alternative would be introducing container-height allocation (bigger change). Acceptable for v1?\n- [ ] **Grid-only scope (defer flex to 029)** — does the leverage argument hold?\n- [ ] **Estimate of 350-400 lines** — acceptable for one cycle, or split into multiple ADRs?\n\n## Deferred (enumerated in ADR)\n\nAll 0-use-on-Wikipedia items: `inline-grid`, `subgrid`, `grid-template` with inline areas, `repeat(N, ...)`, `auto`/`max-content`/`fit-content()`, `grid-auto-*`, line-based `grid-column`/`grid-row`, `fr` row height filling, `min-content` rows (treated as auto), nested grids. Plus flex (ADR-029) and position/float (ADR-030) as their own cycles.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (327 cases, 1367 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/028-grid-layout.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #158\n",
